judge_raw_output:
Analyzer shows modest mean quality gains (+0.0062) but reduced quality variance and an explicit parameter_spread weight of 0.3 that may be delaying further peaks. To prioritize raising quality while keeping some diversity, reduce the spread objective weight.

<decision>{
  "failure_location": "objective",
  "root_cause_hypothesis": "The parameter_spread objective (weight=0.3) is placing non-trivial pressure on solutions to remain diverse; this likely trades off against finding slightly higher-quality, narrower regions. Evidence: quality_score mean 1.8980 (±0.0114) with best=1.9000 and small recent improvement (+0.0062), while parameter_spread mean=0.3791 (±0.0200) — spread is healthy, so its weight can be reduced.",
  "intervention_target": "objective",
  "rationale": "Lowering parameter_spread's weight will let the optimizer concentrate more on increasing quality_score (primary objective) while still preserving some spread (keeping weight >0). This matches the Analyzer recommendation to reduce spread influence when pure quality is the priority.",
  "proposed_change": {
    "ops": [
      {
        "op": "set_weight",
        "name": "parameter_spread",
        "weight": 0.1
      }
    ]
  },
  "expected_benefit": "Shift optimization pressure toward higher-quality solutions, increasing chance of improving the best and mean quality scores in upcoming iterations while retaining moderate diversity (spread still encouraged but less prioritized).",
  "validation_plan": "Validator should compare next-iteration results against the currently accepted state: success if quality_score (mean or best) shows improvement consistent with prioritizing quality (e.g., increase in best quality or a meaningful mean improvement vs. the baseline of 1.8980/ best 1.9000).",
  "confidence": 0.7
}</decision>
